<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  CsCode.app's hardened-runtime entitlements: tools/macos/make-app-bundle.sh signs the app, its apphosts and its libraries with them when it is
  given a Developer ID identity (docs/handoff/macos-audit.md pkg-2 and gap-13; README, "Signing for other Macs").
  * allow-jit: the .NET runtime compiles IL to machine code at run time (MAP_JIT); without it the app dies before its first frame.
  * disable-library-validation: the .NET host loads the runtime's own libraries, and tree-sitter grammars built by the user, Homebrew or Nix
    (cscode.editor.treeSitter) are dylibs signed by no one or by another team; a hardened app refuses to load them otherwise.
  Not granted, because the app runs without them (tests/CsCode.App.Tests MacPackagingTests starts the app's own apphost under the hardened
  runtime with exactly these two, and shows it fails with none): allow-unsigned-executable-memory (.NET maps its JIT code W^X through MAP_JIT,
  which allow-jit covers) and allow-dyld-environment-variables (the app reads no DYLD_* variable).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
